received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-11T07:41:04Z","updated_at":"2026-04-11T07:41:04Z","body":"@swinslow I would argue that the https://spdx.org/licenses/exceptions-index.html stretches the semantics of an exception quite a bit (which I personally do not support); **I'm in favor for clear semantics and isolation of distinct concepts.** \nI still would account an exception that reduces the limitations on a grant - such that the grant is more broad - as an exception. But the addition of permissions beyond those granted by the license it not an exception. \n\nIn the given case here the grant - in my eyes - is on the patent; this is not a topic in the license at all:  \nhttps://github.com/webmproject/libwebm/blob/main/LICENSE.TXT\nhttps://github.com/webmproject/libwebm/blob/main/PATENTS.TXT\n\nFollowing this the given \"Additional IP Rights Grant (Patents)\" it is not an exception; it is a license that can be used as addition:\n`BSD-3-Clause WITH Google-Patent-WebM`\n\nNow we also have the addition-expressions (https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/v3.0.1/annexes/spdx-license-expressions/) we could also use it.\n\nMy proposal was always something more flexible/distinct as conveyed in https://github.com/spdx/change-proposal/blob/main/proposals/Modifiers.md; yet this is currently not available and not event further pursued.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/4228683421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/5700510151","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2613#issuecomment-5700510151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/iss